[Unit]
Description=RANDOM Wikipedia's "Did you know" anecdotes, once a week (Mondays 12:03 Paris: the current and the previous month in French, English and German, the new ones only; after the 11:30 dig, while no small model holds the machine — the next look-alikes are at 12:35 — and between two runs of the previews; a Monday missed is caught up by the next one, which reads the month before too)

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon *-*-* 12:03:00 Europe/Paris
Persistent=false
RandomizedDelaySec=60

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
